+The requested output file remains empty because this run’s filesystem permissions make `docs/plans/` read-only. No files were changed.
+
+1. **P1 — Completion is not the only transition that can unmount a live microphone.** The boxes appear while the queue request is pending ([AddPage.tsx:579](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbkan788-add-page-and-progress/src/web/AddPage.tsx:579)), but disappear when that request returns a public-copy choice or failure ([AddPage.tsx:1550](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbkan788-add-page-and-progress/src/web/AddPage.tsx:1550), [AddPage.tsx:1642](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbkan788-add-page-and-progress/src/web/AddPage.tsx:1642)). Unmount aborts the recording/transcription ([useDictation.ts:2094](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbkan788-add-page-and-progress/src/web/useDictation.ts:2094)); recovery is best-effort and can be unavailable ([dictation-keep.ts:27](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbkan788-add-page-and-progress/src/web/dictation-keep.ts:27)). Keep both boxes mounted while either is busy across public-copy, refusal and source transitions, and withhold public-copy navigation until dictation ends.
+
+2. **P1 — A busy ref alone cannot implement the promised Open-button guard.** Child hook state does not rerender `ReadyBar`, so its buttons could remain visibly enabled. Two fields also cannot safely share one last-writer-wins boolean. Use separate purpose/About-you refs for same-tick guards plus parent state for rendering their OR. Guard and disable both copies of **Open the article**, the purpose Cmd/Ctrl+Enter path ([AddPage.tsx:1659](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbkan788-add-page-and-progress/src/web/AddPage.tsx:1659)), and **Open without saving** ([AddPage.tsx:1520](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbkan788-add-page-and-progress/src/web/AddPage.tsx:1520)). The waiting effect must also refuse to leave while busy ([AddPage.tsx:1494](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbkan788-add-page-and-progress/src/web/AddPage.tsx:1494)). Disable both microphones once Open is waiting, preventing “Open, then start dictating before the PATCH answers.”
+
+3. **P1 — Dictation can currently save Chromium’s rough live guesses before the authoritative transcript.** Live confirmed phrases go through ordinary `onChange` before being replaced by the final transcript ([useDictationField.ts:377](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbkan788-add-page-and-progress/src/web/useDictationField.ts:377)). `ProfileBox` pauses autosave for precisely this reason ([ProfileBox.tsx:225](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbkan788-add-page-and-progress/src/web/ProfileBox.tsx:225)), whereas `AboutYouBox` currently hard-codes `paused: false` ([AddPage.tsx:2133](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbkan788-add-page-and-progress/src/web/AddPage.tsx:2133)). Purpose has its own timer ([add-purpose.ts:478](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbkan788-add-page-and-progress/src/web/add-purpose.ts:478)), and an unseeded session immediately commits its current text when the read lands ([add-purpose.ts:448](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbkan788-add-page-and-progress/src/web/add-purpose.ts:448)). Pause About-you autosave and add a purpose-session dictation pause covering both its timer and seed-triggered commit; unpause and commit only after `onEnd`.
+
+4. **P1 — The keeper key is dangerously underspecified.** The plan says “box and source,” but `source` is empty for every upload; `wanted` is the normalized URL or upload id ([AddPage.tsx:654](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbkan788-add-page-and-progress/src/web/AddPage.tsx:654), [AddPage.tsx:704](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbkan788-add-page-and-progress/src/web/AddPage.tsx:704)). Using `source` would collide all upload-purpose recordings. Specify names such as `add:purpose:${wanted}` and source-independent `add:about-you`; About you is one global field and should not require revisiting the same article to recover it. Do not include the reader id: recovery is already reader-partitioned ([dictation-keep.ts:390](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbkan788-add-page-and-progress/src/web/dictation-keep.ts:390)).
+
+5. **P2 — `{kind:"profile"}` is correct for About you, but unnecessarily weak for Purpose once a slug exists.** The article recipe adds purpose, glossary, title, author and proper nouns; profile supplies only site/profile terms ([vocabulary-sources.ts:383](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbkan788-add-page-and-progress/src/vocabulary-sources.ts:383)). Use article context with `job?.slug ?? completion?.slug`, falling back to profile before a slug exists. Context is snapshotted when recording starts, so a later slug change is safe ([useDictation.ts:805](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbkan788-add-page-and-progress/src/web/useDictation.ts:805)).
