@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+/* button-tone.css — **green to send, red to leave without sending.** The pair
+   of buttons that ends a form: the one that sends what you wrote is
+   `.tone-positive`, the one that backs out is `.tone-negative`. Greg,
+   2026-10-19 (`spya-as0et6`): "color the buttons red and green, and for close
+   as well, just so it's easier to see what's … effectively a cancel and what's
+   a submit … update our design system". Plan 261020f; first drawn as the
+   Feedback thread's Send reply and Defer for now (261011h).
+
+   **What red means here is narrow**: leave, or put off, without sending. Not
+   "destructive" — Feedback's Cancel and Close keep the draft. An act that
+   loses something is the `--destructive` fill (shadcn's destructive Button).
+   The words carry the meaning and the colour is a shortcut, as
+   colour-scales.md asks of a red/green pair.
+
+   **Colour only**: the text and the border take it, at rest and on hover.
+   Shape, size and padding stay the family's own. **No wash behind**: a tint
+   of the same hue takes the light theme under the 4.5:1 that
+   tests/appearance-palette.test.ts holds both tokens to (GPT Sol, 261011h).
+
+   **Imported last in styles.css, and the selectors cover every state that
+   could repaint a toned button** — rest, hover, and `.fb-copy`'s unavailable
+   hover — so each matches-and-follows or outweighs it.
+   tests/feedback-dialog-styles.test.ts holds the inventory. */
+
+.tone-positive,
+.tone-positive:hover,
+.tone-positive[aria-disabled="true"]:hover {
+  color: var(--positive);
+  border-color: currentColor;
+}
+.tone-negative,
+.tone-negative:hover,
+.tone-negative[aria-disabled="true"]:hover {
+  color: var(--danger);
+  border-color: currentColor;
+}
+/* **Coloured and unpressable reads as pressable**, so it dims — unless it is
+   working (a spinner and a word that change), which is not "cannot be
+   pressed" (plan 261019c). */
+.tone-positive:disabled,
+.tone-negative:disabled {
+  opacity: 0.45;
+  cursor: default;
+}
+.tone-positive[data-working]:disabled,
+.tone-negative[data-working]:disabled {
+  opacity: 1;
+  cursor: progress;
+}
